    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald Radford is delighted to bring to the market this exceptionally well-presented detached home, superbly situated on the outskirts of the village of Taghmon and just a 10-minute drive from Wexford Town.\n\nOriginally a much-loved family home, the property has been completely transformed by the current owners over the past four years. With considerable care, investment and attention to detail, they have seamlessly married the original cottage with a beautifully designed extension, creating a warm, contemporary and highly functional home that combines character with all the comforts of modern living.\n\nPresented with considerable flair, the house has been comprehensively renovated and upgraded throughout. The works include a stunning open-plan kitchen/dining room, quality sanitary ware, a stylish ensuite, new plumbing and electrics, flooring, doors and windows, together with numerous other improvements that have resulted in a home of exceptional presentation and comfort.\n\nThe accommodation briefly comprises an entrance hall, shower room, three bedrooms, main ensuite, living room, rear hall and impressive open-plan kitchen/dining room. The house has been thoughtfully designed to maximise both natural light and everyday functionality, while retaining the charm and character of the original dwelling including high ceilings.\n\nSet on approximately 0.89 acres, the property enjoys generous grounds with excellent potential for those seeking additional space and privacy. The gardens are predominantly laid in lawn and are beautifully enclosed by mature hedging and established trees, creating a wonderfully private and secluded setting. There is also extensive off-street parking surrounding the property.\n\nThe property had planning permission granted in 2009 for an additional house on the site. This permission has now lapsed; however, the generous site may offer potential for future development, subject to the necessary planning permission and the purchaser satisfying themselves in this regard.\n\nThe location is particularly appealing. Taghmon village is close by for everyday amenities, while Wexford Town is approximately 10 minutes away by car. The property's position also provides easy access to the main routes serving Dublin, Waterford and beyond. For those who enjoy the coast, the beautiful beaches and coastal amenities of Kilmore Quay, Duncannon and Bannow Bay are all within easy driving distance."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 2.12m x 0.95m\nTiled floor, hatch to attic\n\nShower Room - 2.48m x 1.98m\nSuite comprising fully tiled shower unit with \"Triton T90\" shower, wc, wash hand basin with storage, wall hung mirror with lighting, chrome towel rail, hotpress, tiled floor, part tiled walls\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.58m x 2.38m\nWindow to the side, laminate flooring\n\nLiving Room - 4.49m x 3.43m\nPicture window to front, laminate flooring, feature electric fire, feature panelled wall\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.5m x 2.99m\nDual aspect to front and side, laminate flooring\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.88m x 2.83m\nPicture window to side, laminate flooring\n\nEnsuite - 2.7m x 1.01m\nFully tiled suite comprising step in shower with \"Triton Novel sr\" shower, wc, wash hand basin with storage, wall hung mirror with light chrome towel rail\n\nRear Hall - 2.33m x 1.13m + 2.81m x 0.99m\nDoor to side, tiled floor\n\nKitchen / Dining Room - 5m x 3.93m\nFitted wall and floor units, worktop with integrated sink and drainer, dishwasher, tiled splashback, washing machine, Rangemaster Classic free standing dual fuel cooker with gas hob and electric oven, American style fridge/ freezer, laminate floor, wood effect tiled flooring\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Stunning completely rennovated and extended detached three bedroom cottage</li><li>Large site with potential to develop further (subject to planning permission)</li><li>Oil fired central heating</li><li>Rennovated in the last 4 years</li><li>Newly installed plumbing</li><li>Newly installed electrics</li><li>Newly installed roof</li><li>Full replaster inside and out</li><li>Double glazed windows throughout</li><li>Composite door to front and side</li><li>Fully insulated internally</li><li>Off street parking</li><li>Septic tank</li><li>Mains water</ul>"
      },
